\title{PsychoMatic: automated psychometric workflows}
\description{
\code{PsychoMatic} provides low-syntax, reproducible workflows for declaring and
checking psychometric data, scoring, reliability, exploratory and
confirmatory factor analysis, exploratory structural equation measurement
models, psychometric networks, complete and researcher-directed partial
measurement invariance, alignment, IRT/DIF screening, auditing, and reports.
Automation reduces procedural syntax but does not replace measurement theory,
design decisions, or substantive review.
}
\details{
Use \code{\link[=psychomatic_spec]{psychomatic_spec()}} when item roles or
encodings should be explicit. Main analysis functions include
\code{\link[=desc_auto]{desc_auto()}}, \code{\link[=score_scale]{score_scale()}}, \code{\link[=reliability_auto]{reliability_auto()}}, \code{\link[=cormat]{cormat()}},
\code{\link[=efa_auto]{efa_auto()}}, \code{\link[=cfa_auto]{cfa_auto()}}, \code{\link[=esem_auto]{esem_auto()}},
\code{\link[=network_auto]{network_auto()}}, \code{\link[=network_plots]{network_plots()}},
\code{\link[=factorial_invariance_auto]{factorial_invariance_auto()}}, \code{\link[=ordinal_invariance_auto]{ordinal_invariance_auto()}},
\code{\link[=invariance_partial]{invariance_partial()}}, \code{\link[=inv_align_auto]{inv_align_auto()}},
\code{\link[=irt_auto]{irt_auto()}}, \code{\link[=dif_auto]{dif_auto()}}, and \code{\link[=compare_models_auto]{compare_models_auto()}}. Use
\code{\link[=psychomatic_report]{psychomatic_report()}} for explicit export.

Most 1.0.0 analysis objects inherit from \code{psychomatic_result} and separate
requested/effective settings, raw results, structured conditions,
diagnostics, decisions, and conclusions. Numerical analysis fields retain
full precision; display and report formatting may honor \code{digits}.

Ordinal encodings, missing-data policies, estimator/identification settings,
and \code{not_evaluable} states should always be inspected. Fit cutoffs, parallel
analysis, Chen fit-change thresholds, DIF flags, and alignment summaries are
decision aids rather than formal proof of validity or invariance.
